==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|ka-blooey}}, {{l|en|ka-blooie}}
* {{l|en|kablooey}}
* {{l|en|kerblooie}}, {{l|en|kerplooie}}

===Etymology===
[[ka-]], an [[intensifier]] used with onomatopoeia, plus (probably) an imaginative rendition of an explosion or splash.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-us-kablooie.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{lb|en|colloquial}} A [[failure]], [[meltdown]]; or [[explosion]]; a [[splat]] or [[splash]].
#: ''The bottle of ketchup hit the floor and went '''kablooie''' all over everything.''

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{alternative spelling of|en|kablooey}}.

===Interjection===
{{en-interj}}

# {{alternative spelling of|en|kablooey}}.

====Usage notes====
Most frequently used in the phrase '''to go kablooie''' or ''' it went kablooie'''.

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|blooey}}

